# Parameters for the tilt-tricopter bridge flight, applied ON TOP of
# ArduPilot's plane.parm + quadplane.parm + quadplane-tilttri.parm defaults.
# The servo map is pinned explicitly so the vehicle YAML never guesses.
ARMING_CHECK 0
BATT_MONITOR 4
Q_M_SPIN_ARM 0.02
SERVO1_FUNCTION 4
SERVO2_FUNCTION 19
SERVO3_FUNCTION 0
SERVO4_FUNCTION 21
SERVO5_FUNCTION 33
SERVO6_FUNCTION 34
SERVO7_FUNCTION 0
SERVO8_FUNCTION 36
SERVO11_FUNCTION 39
SERVO12_FUNCTION 41
# ── Powertrain-matched speeds ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The demo flies a fine-pitch hover prop (10x4.7, pitch speed ~15 m/s at
# flyable rpm). The quadplane DEFAULTS assume a plane prop — cruise 25,
# assist below 18 — speeds this powertrain cannot hold: TECS porpoises
# trading altitude for airspeed, and assisted flight flaps in and out around
# 18 m/s, keeping the rear lift rotor spinning in fast edgewise flow the
# whole flight. Cruise at 13 with assist below 9 keeps the wing loaded, the
# tilted front rotors inside their sampled axial envelope, and the rear
# rotor genuinely stopped in cruise — wing-borne flight is the point of the
# example. Retune these when you change the propeller.
AIRSPEED_CRUISE 13
AIRSPEED_MIN 10
AIRSPEED_MAX 18
Q_ASSIST_SPEED 9
